# S5-07 post-CPL3 IRQ fix counted N=2 series, 2026-11-15

Purpose: re-run the same counted Stage 4 nonce workload after S4-39h added
external IRQ delivery from CPL3 through TSS.RSP0, and inspect repeatability
without changing comparator policy.

## Inputs and runner

- Worktree: `codex`; production source revision `d50ddc993cd3817fdca7e9770d9d0e2de69382ee`; `source_dirty=false`.
- Host: macOS, `aarch64`; `od-runner` 0.1.0, release build.
- Kernel SHA-256: `9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e`.
- Initramfs SHA-256: `ee9183a4eded3c16a8c6a7a81c6d5bb79be8bb023f793f7cd61694ea2bd3e588`.
- ACPI blob SHA-256: `b1ba6078a4d9bc7a8d224980713d8242e4a708743ce4f56093b00a07c631ffaf`.
- Scenario `stage4-init-nonce`, profile `smoke_not_acceptance`, counted
  `stage4a --set-cpl0 --user-mode`, RAM 128 MiB, budget 3,000,000,000,
  expected stop `budget_exhausted`; one series ID, two unique run nonces.

## Run outcomes

Aggregate outcome: `passed`. Both runs started the guest, emitted the exact
nonce marker, exited 0 at `budget_exhausted`, and retired 2,999,999,998
instructions; each reported 1,093 CPL3 retired instructions.

| Run | Nonce | Guest exceptions delivered | IRQs / IRQ0 edges | Wall seconds |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
| 0001 | `OD518e81cb70da22650000064f400000000` | 35 | 34,813 / 34,808 | 1114.1376 |
| 0002 | `OD518e81dba778fd0b8000064f400000001` | 34 | 34,837 / 34,832 | 1115.6188 |

`exceptions_delivered` counts successful guest `#PF` and `#GP(0)` deliveries
through the guest IDT; it is not an IRQ count. The run record does not preserve
the vector breakdown, so the observed totals cannot be attributed to one vector.

## Strict comparisons

- Comparing the two runs from this series: `matches=false`; unexplained
  differences are `run[0].machine_observations differs` and
  `run[0].ordered_uart_bytes differs after nonce normalization`.
- The pre-fix 2026-11-15 diagnostic N=2 series also fails its internal
  comparison on those same two categories. Thus this run does not show a new
  comparator failure introduced by the CPL3 IRQ fix, and it does not explain
  the underlying run-to-run variation.
- Comparing this series with the earlier failed common-ID C series returns
  `matches=false`; the old C failure remains historical failed evidence and
  was not reproduced here.
- No comparator normalization was broadened: the one-count guest exception
  difference (without a vector breakdown) and remaining ordered UART difference
  have not been shown to be benign.

These observations do not satisfy S5-07 acceptance. The old failure was not
observed in these two runs, but its cause remains unlocalized and strict
within-series repeatability still fails.

